## Reviewer points not followed

- Zero-width lines are in the Korean source, not only in the Malay. Deleting them fails the block checker.
- Q16–Q20 are body lines in the Korean and English articles as well. Turning them into headings would change the heading-level sequence.
- Heading “7” after “5” is the source outline. Changing it to 6 changes a counted digit.
- The difficulty table row cannot be removed without changing the table-row count. The cells were rewritten so they no longer read as an easy dismissal or an easy severance.
- One clause per paragraph in 013 and 015 matches the Korean block count. Merging them would fail the checker. The “dan soalan…” opener in 013 was repaired without merging blocks.
- The suggested 012 sentence names Malaysia. The nationality check treats Malaysia as a reader-country token, and R2 says not to add a claim about the reader’s law. The page now states the Taiwan fact only: vehicles keep to the right, so passing is on the left.
- The suggested 018 denial “perundingan bahasa Melayu tidak ditawarkan” matches the forbidden-phrase rule that flags “perundingan dalam bahasa Melayu” as an offer of Malay consultation. The negative formula already used in the pack was used instead.
- The suggested guidance sentence uses “percuma”. The Malay pack test forbids that token even inside a denial. The sentence says “tanpa bayaran” instead, which is the word the same paragraph already uses.
- Dropping the digit from “1 kali ganda” would risk a missing-number failure. “ganda” was the error (sekali ganda means double). Ordinary negligence now reads “sehingga 1 kali jumlah kerugian sebenar”.
